  "literature_notes": "Three ledger lines were examined. L1 and L2 (PMC3103399) both describe a mouse TRPC6-HA construct confirmed at the cell surface by biotinylation, proving the HA tag is extracellularly accessible. However, neither clip names a residue, a loop, or even a domain where the tag was inserted. TRPC6 has no extracellular terminus (both N-terminus, residues 1\u2013402, and C-terminus, residues 723\u2013931, are intracellular), so the topology_derived rule (requiring exactly one extracellular terminus) cannot be applied. The named-loop rule also cannot be applied because no loop is named. The position is therefore fully unstated, and per the rules a plasmid whose tag position is unstated cannot be pinned to insert_after_residue. L3 (PMC10014292) describes a TRPC6-YFP fusion protein; standard fusion nomenclature places YFP at the C-terminus (after residue 931), which is intracellular (topology span 723\u2013931). This is an intracellular tag and is recorded in other_positions. No ledger line supports a surface tag site with a pinnable position.",
